# QA M5 regression (D-090 top clamp; was
# qa_m5_bug_perch_bounce_lake_off_screen): after a stomp bounce from the
# Zaunerstollen perch the lake stays on screen. The bug: as Zuckerschock
# (qa_m5_wolfgangsee_relaxed's inputs) Resi stomps Gelse #3 from the perch
# (row 8); the bounce took her top to y 35 and the dead zone pulled the
# camera to y 0 (3710-3792, below 24 until ~3815), so the swim water
# (surface y 192) left the screen while she stepped off into the lake, and
# swan #3 (hitbox y 184-196) only became fully on screen, and telegraphed,
# when the camera came down again (3801). Now the auto-scroll camera never
# goes above y 24 (D-090): the water line stays at screen y <= 168 and
# every swan and regatta keel that is horizontally on screen is fully on
# screen. In this run the camera holds at 24 from 3696 to the end
# (frames 3696-3800, except 2 px during the second hop) and swan #3
# telegraphs on the frame after its hitbox is first horizontally inside
# the screen (3795), as with the camera at rest. Inputs as before, except on the perch she walks 2 frames
# more and waits 2 less (R 16, - 19; was R 14, - 21) to stand clear of the
# row-5 Z-box (D-090), which a standing jump would bump otherwise; the
# second hop (3756) now passes beside the perch bollard instead of landing
# on it. The replay format can't check the camera:
# `tests::lake::the_perch_bounce_keeps_the_lake_on_screen` replays this
# file and checks camera y >= 24 on every frame and the swan; the regatta
# trigger frames on a masthead bounce are checked on the solver route
# (`tests::lake::masthead_bounces_never_delay_a_regatta_start`). The shots
# become goldens after art-director review.
level  = wolfgangsee
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
expect = deaths=0 no_event=Hurt event=Stomped power=big
shots  = 3725:stomp_bounce_top 3760:perch_hop 3790:drop_into_lake
